 "notes": "PORTFOLIO (CV-agg | holdout): policy [net +1.76%/20d, naive Sharpe +1.38, turnover 29%/d | net +4.67%/20d, naive Sharpe +3.43, turnover 27%/d]; random20 [net +1.58%/20d, naive Sharpe +2.19, turnover 99%/d | net +1.53%/20d, naive Sharpe +2.26, turnover 99%/d]; mom20 [net +2.71%/20d, naive Sharpe +1.53, turnover 23%/d | net +5.15%/20d, naive Sharpe +6.32, turnover 22%/d]. Rewards are overlapping 20-session excess returns vs the universe MEDIAN sampled daily (not compounded); the cross-section is right-skewed, so even random-20 earns a positive mean -- the bar is beating random, not zero. HONEST ASSESSMENT: (a) does the learned policy beat random-20 out of sample? yes on both CV and holdout on mean net reward (CV-agg +1.76% vs random +1.58%; holdout +4.67% vs +1.53%); (b) vs the cs_rank_mom_20 heuristic: no on both (heuristic holdout +5.15%). On the classifier lens the policy scores cv_auc 0.5085 +/- 0.0217 (fold range 0.483-0.538) and holdout 0.5680, trailing the supervised family (LGBM top-10: cv 0.5307, holdout 0.5219; logistic cv ~0.513) -- REINFORCE is at best recovering the same weak, regime-unstable momentum/vol tilt the supervised rankers already capture, through a far noisier gradient estimator. Six months of EOD data (~190-280 episodes per fold, one noisy scalar reward each) is NOT enough for RL here: early stopping picked epochs 0-12 across folds, and inner-validation reward curves were dominated by regime noise, so the variance of the policy-gradient estimate swamps the ~0.52-AUC signal. The one thing the bandit objective adds -- turnover-aware selection -- does not need RL: a supervised ranker plus a portfolio constructor with a turnover penalty (or simple score-hysteresis) achieves it deterministically. RL would start earning its complexity only with multi-step position management (entries/exits, holding-period and path-dependent costs), a realistic cost/impact model that depends on the agent's own actions, regime/state features, and years of cross-sectional history (thousands of episodes); none of those hold in this 6-month EOD pilot. Verdict: do not scale this RL formulation; if portfolio-level objectives matter, bolt a constructor onto the supervised rankers and judge those on regime stability, per the linear report.",
